ge":null,"text":"62,297 ","origin":[5,3],"resolved_text":"62,297 ","footnote_ids":[]},{"cell":4,"col":4,"span":1,"vmerge":null,"text":"180,667 ","origin":[5,4],"resolved_text":"180,667 ","footnote_ids":[]},{"cell":5,"col":5,"span":1,"vmerge":null,"text":"60,222 ","origin":[5,5],"resolved_text":"60,222 ","footnote_ids":[]},{"cell":6,"col":6,"span":1,"vmerge":null,"text":" ","origin":[5,6],"resolved_text":" ","footnote_ids":[]},{"cell":7,"col":7,"span":1,"vmerge":null,"text":"45,167 ","origin":[5,7],"resolved_text":"45,167 ","footnote_ids":[]},{"cell":8,"col":8,"span":1,"vmerge":null,"text":" ","origin":[5,8],"resolved_text":" ","footnote_ids":[]},{"cell":9,"col":9,"span":1,"vmerge":null,"text":"$1,544,574 ","origin":[5,9],"resolved_text":"$1,544,574 ","footnote_ids":[]}],"grid":["Total","58,186 ","60,184 ","62,297 ","180,667 ","60,222 "," ","45,167 "," ","$1,544,574 "]}],"issues":[]},{"table":1,"context":["There are two categories of respondents: flight training candidates and flight training providers. TSA estimates a total of 39,496 respondents annually: 19,869 flight training candidates and 19,627 flight training providers.  Non-U.S. citizens and non-U.S. national candidates are required to provide or update the biographical and biometric information as well as information on the training itself each time they apply for flight training as described in 49 CFR part 1552.  ","TSA estimates the average annual number of flight training events to be 40,340 for Category 1, 2, or 3 and 19,882 for Category 4.  TSA estimates it takes 45 minutes (0.75 hours) per training request application, and uses a hourly compensation rate of $34.20 for all flight training candidates. TSA multiplies the number of training events by the hourly burden per training event and candidate compensation rate to calculate the annual hour burden cost. Table 1 summarizes the burden for flight training candidates.","Flight training providers must retain candidate training records for each flight training event. TSA estimates that it will take small or independent provides, such as CFI and flying club providers, 5 minutes (0.083 hours) to file candidate records and 1 hour for large providers. Additionally, all flight training providers are required to maintain employees’ security awareness training record, which TSA estimates takes 5 minutes (0.083 hours). For both candidate and employee records, TSA uses the $62.33 compensation rate for CFI and flying club providers’ and the $28.80 compensation rate for large providers’ to calculate the total hour burden cost. Table 2 summarizes these burdens."],"grid_columns":11,"rows":[{"row":0,"cells":[{"cell":0,"col":0,"span":11,"vmerge":null,"text":"Table 2.  Training Recordkeeping Costs","origin":[0,0],"resolved_text":"Table 2.  Training Recordkeeping Costs","footnote_ids":[]}],"grid":["Table 2.  Training Recordkeeping Costs","Table 2.  Training Recordkeeping Costs","Table 2.  Training Recordkeeping Costs","Table 2.  Training Recordkeeping Costs","Table 2.  Training Recordkeeping Costs","Table 2.  Training Recordkeeping Costs","Table 2.  Training Recordkeeping Costs","Table 2.  Training Recordkeeping Costs","Table 2.  Training Recordkeeping Costs","Table 2.  Training Recordkeeping Costs","Table 2.  Training Recordkeeping Costs"]},{"row":1,"cells":[{"cell":0,"col":0,"span":2,"vmerge":"restart","text":"Training Activity","origin":[1,0],"resolved_text":"Training Activity","footnote_ids":[]},{"cell":1,"col":2,"span":4,"vmerge":null,"text":"Records","origin":[1,1],"resolved_text":"Records","footnote_ids":[]},{"cell":2,"col":6,"span":1,"vmerge":null,"text":"Average\nAnnual Records","origin":[1,2],"resolved_text":"Average\nAnnual Records","footnote_ids":[]},{"cell":3,"col":7,"span":1,"vmerge":null,"text":"Hour Burden Per Record","origin":[1,3],"resolved_text":"Hour Burden Per Record","footnote_ids":[]},{"cell":4,"col":8,"span":1,"vmerge":null,"text":"Total Hour Burden","origin":[1,4],"resolved_text":"Total Hour Burden","footnote